"""Dump V2 ownership-evidence change scope: the exact edits Dump V2 made to the
firmware YAML - the on_boot lambda, three Dump scripts, two added RAM globals -
and to firmware/include/ecco_durable_snapshot.h, as (before, after) text pairs.

Same technique as _sg06_scope.py. Earlier suites (SG-01 Phase 0/5, SG-06) pin
on_boot, the durable header, every script body and the globals byte-for-byte
as change-scope proofs. Dump V2 necessarily edits some of them. Rather than
re-pinning those suites to new hashes - which would silently widen what they
accept - they hash the current text with exactly these edits reverted. Every
`after` must occur exactly once (else AssertionError), so any OTHER change
still breaks those pins, and registry/tests/test_dump_v2_ownership_evidence.py
pins that each revert reproduces main @ 004040b (the Dump V2 base) exactly.
pre_dump_v2_firmware() also lets that suite rebuild the base firmware without
git history and run it side by side with the V2 firmware (differential tests).

Generated from the real diff against 004040b and verified by round trip; the
on_boot pairs are in the parsed (YAML-dedented) lambda form, the script pairs
in raw script-body form (_free_power_action_sim.script_body), the firmware
pairs in raw LF-newline file form. No I/O.
"""

